 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Depends on the number of epochs and points per ray. Reconstruction stage uses 6 epochs with 192 points/ray; stylization uses 4 epochs [S3].
+- **Time Complexity:** Depends on the number of epochs and points per ray [S3]. Reconstruction stage uses 6 epochs with 192 points/ray; stylization uses 4 epochs [S3].
 - **Memory Complexity:** Reduced by processing at the patch level (1/10 of original input) for local contrastive loss [S3].
 - **Strengths:** Balances local pixel fidelity with global structural integrity and perceptual quality [S3].
-- **Limitations:** Requires manual collection of negative text samples. Adversarial loss is critical for style transfer; removing it degrades quality significantly [S4].
+- **Limitations:** Requires manual collection of negative text samples [S3]. Adversarial loss is critical for style transfer; removing it degrades quality significantly [S4].
 - **When to use:** When high-fidelity stylization of radiance fields is required using text guidance [S3].
 - **When not to use:** When computational resources are extremely limited or when style transfer is not needed (use standard reconstruction loss) [S3].
 
 ## Background
-The method is based on NeRF-Art [S3], which introduces text-driven neural radiance fields stylization. It builds on VolSDF [S3] as the base NeRF model. The approach addresses the limitations of single-metric losses in generating visually consistent stylized images. The "No conditional adversarial objective" variant is discussed in Pix2NeRF [S4] to highlight the role of adversarial training in conditional GANs for NeRF translation.
